{{!--
  Module switcher — the side menu shows one module's navigation at a time
  (nav-menu.hbs), and this is what moves between them. It stands in for what
  Fumadocs rendered as a `RootToggle` in its sidebar's banner slot, and sits
  in the same place: below the brand block, above the tree.

  Only renders for a component that actually has several annotated modules.
  `page.navigation.[1]` is the "more than one root menu" test (the same
  `.[1]` trick page-versions.hbs uses for "more than one version"), and the
  `module` check is "…and something annotated them", i.e.
  @inditextech/pdocs-antora-extensions is registered and the descriptor
  declares `nav_modules`. A single-nav-file site — starter, the CLI template —
  fails both and renders nothing at all here.

  `title`, `description`, `icon` and `startUrl` are all stamped onto the tree
  by that extension; Antora's own navigation model has no notion of any of
  them. `icon` is a `<group>/<name>` reference into the vendored sprite, split
  here because the {{icon}} helper takes the two separately.

  The trigger is a button, not a link: it opens the panel, and the panel is
  what navigates. Its label is the ACTIVE module, so the control reads as
  "you are in X, pick another" rather than as an unlabelled menu.

  "Active" is the module whose tree the side menu is actually showing, which
  is `:page-nav-module:` where a page sets one — see nav-menu.hbs. A landing
  borrowing `main`'s navigation therefore reads as being in `main`, rather
  than labelling itself with a module it does not belong to.

  A tree with no `startUrl` is not offered at all: that is either a module
  whose navigation has no internal page to link to, or a menu declared
  `switcher: false` — a landing's own navigation, which is not a module and
  must not appear beside the real ones.
--}}
{{#if (and page.navigation.[1] page.navigation.[0].module)}}
<div class="nav-switcher">
  {{#each page.navigation}}
  {{#if (eq ./module (or @root.page.attributes.[nav-module] @root.page.module))}}
  <button class="nav-switcher__toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="Switch module, currently {{detag ./title}}">
    {{#with (split ./icon '/')}}
    <span class="nav-switcher__icon">{{icon this.[0] this.[1]}}</span>
    {{/with}}
    <span class="nav-switcher__label">
      <span class="nav-switcher__title ids-text ids-text--body-m-high">{{{./title}}}</span>
      {{#with ./description}}
      <span class="nav-switcher__description ids-text ids-text--detail-m">{{{this}}}</span>
      {{/with}}
    </span>
    <span class="nav-switcher__chevron">{{icon "arrows" "chevron-down-outlined"}}</span>
  </button>
  {{/if}}
  {{/each}}
  <div class="nav-switcher__menu" hidden>
    <ul class="ids-list nav-switcher__list">
      {{#each page.navigation}}
      {{#if ./startUrl}}
      <li class="nav-switcher__item">
        <a class="nav-switcher__option" href="{{{relativize ./startUrl}}}"
          {{~#if (eq ./module (or @root.page.attributes.[nav-module] @root.page.module))}} aria-current="true"{{/if~}}>
          {{#with (split ./icon '/')}}
          <span class="nav-switcher__icon">{{icon this.[0] this.[1]}}</span>
          {{/with}}
          <span class="nav-switcher__label">
            <span class="nav-switcher__title ids-text ids-text--body-m-high">{{{./title}}}</span>
            {{#with ./description}}
            <span class="nav-switcher__description ids-text ids-text--detail-m">{{{this}}}</span>
            {{/with}}
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {{/if}}
      {{/each}}
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
{{/if}}
